From: Isaiah <isaiahdw@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: sunxi_wdt: adopt a bootloader-enabled watchdog

The probe unconditionally stopped the watchdog, so a watchdog armed
by the bootloader (U-Boot WATCHDOG_AUTOSTART) was disabled before the
watchdog core could take it over, leaving the whole pre-userspace boot
unguarded. If the mode register shows the watchdog running, mark it
WDOG_HW_RUNNING and leave it alone so the core keeps it alive
(WATCHDOG_HANDLE_BOOT_ENABLED) until userspace opens the device, and
resets if that never happens (WATCHDOG_OPEN_TIMEOUT). A boot hang before
the watchdog daemon starts is then caught and recovered.
---
--- a/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
@@ -286,7 +286,20 @@
 
 	watchdog_set_drvdata(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev, sunxi_wdt);
 
-	sunxi_wdt_stop(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
+	/*
+	 * If the bootloader already started the watchdog (U-Boot
+	 * WATCHDOG_AUTOSTART), adopt it instead of stopping it: mark it running
+	 * so the core keeps pinging it (WATCHDOG_HANDLE_BOOT_ENABLED) until
+	 * userspace opens the device, and resets the board if that never
+	 * happens (WATCHDOG_OPEN_TIMEOUT). This guards the pre-userspace boot
+	 * window; a hang before the watchdog daemon starts is otherwise never
+	 * caught.
+	 */
+	if (readl(sunxi_wdt->wdt_base + sunxi_wdt->wdt_regs->wdt_mode) &
+	    WDT_MODE_EN)
+		set_bit(WDOG_HW_RUNNING, &sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev.status);
+	else
+		sunxi_wdt_stop(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
 
 	watchdog_stop_on_reboot(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
 	err = devm_watchdog_register_device(dev, &sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
